<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. *@
    <meta name="description" content="bit Bcrdt (Bit.Bcrdt) - real-time collaborative editing for .NET and Blazor, written natively in C#: a CRDT engine for text, lists, maps and sets, a synchronization protocol, presence, offline-first persistence and selective undo, with no JavaScript CRDT library." />

    @* Link previews: the card a chat client or a social site unfurls is the first impression a
       shared link makes - and the live page is made to be shared. *@
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bit.Bcrdt" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bcrdt - real-time collaboration for .NET and Blazor" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="A CRDT engine, sync, presence, offline-first persistence and selective undo, written in C# - no JavaScript CRDT library, no interop in the engine." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://bcrdt.bitplatform.dev/icon-512.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />

    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The site kit (app.css, theme.js, site.js - shared by every Utilities demo), then this demo's
       own sample styles. The library ships no stylesheet: its components render plain markup, and
       the one script BcrdtTextArea needs is imported on demand. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["demo.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-CSS bundle: includes the client project's *.razor.css files as well. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Bit.Bcrdt.Demo.Server.styles.css"]" />
    @* Synchronous on purpose: applies the light/dark theme before first paint. *@
    <script src="@Assets["theme.js"]"></script>
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="512x512" href="icon-512.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

@* data-enhance-nav="false": a link followed before the WebAssembly runtime has started is a plain
   page load rather than an enhanced one. Enhanced navigation fetches and merges the next page while
   the runtime is still starting, and the router the runtime then attaches can render the address
   it read before the merge - the URL says /getting-started and the page is the landing page. Once the
   app is interactive its router handles every link itself and this attribute is not consulted. *@
<body data-enhance-nav="false">
    @* InteractiveWebAssembly rather than Auto or Server: every replica on a demo page is a separate document in the
       browser's own memory, talking to its peers over the library's in-memory transport, so nothing has to cross the
       network to be merged. The pages are still prerendered, so the first response carries the explanations. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">&#128473;</span>
    </div>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["site.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
